; presets/veteran.eval — a mid-game party: trained, armed and armoured.
;
; A single eval run cannot play from fresh characters to end-game, so a rung
; that wants to measure mid-game combat has to START there. This is that seed.
;
; The numbers are a FIRST CUT and are meant to move — the point of a preset is
; that "what mid-game means" lives in one editable file instead of being spread
; across every script that wanted it.

echo preset veteran: trained, armed and armoured

; --- stats ---------------------------------------------------------------
; Roughly double the starting spread. RecomputeMaxima re-derives hp/stamina/mana
; from these, so the order here does not matter but the setting of them does —
; a seeded skill on unseeded stats is a veteran with a novice's hit points.
setstat 0 str 18
setstat 0 dex 16
setstat 0 vit 18
setstat 1 str 14
setstat 1 dex 20
setstat 1 vit 15
setstat 2 str 12
setstat 2 dex 15
setstat 2 vit 14
setstat 2 wil 18
setstat 3 dex 14
setstat 3 wil 20
setstat 3 int 20

; --- skills --------------------------------------------------------------
; Levels derive from floor(sqrt(xp)), so `setskill` squares what it is given.
; The front rank fights, the back rank casts; `avoid` is the unarmoured-only
; defensive loop, so the armoured members below are given little of it.
setskill 0 blade 8
setskill 0 blunt 6
setskill 0 unarmed 4
setskill 1 blade 9
setskill 1 avoid 7
setskill 2 fire 6
setskill 2 earth 5
setskill 2 avoid 4
setskill 3 fire 9
setskill 3 water 7
setskill 3 air 5

; --- gear ----------------------------------------------------------------
; `equip` reaches a hand, `wear` reaches the doll — worn armour only counts on
; the doll (DungeonWorld::WornArmorClass).
equip serrated_blade 0 0
equip club 0 1
equip flamebrand 1 0
wear plate_cuirass 0
wear leather_armor 1
